  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Foslevodopa (combined with a decarboxylase inhibitor) is an anti-Parkinson drug belonging to the dopa derivatives, used to treat Parkinson's disease. It is an approved medicine, though detailed information on where and how widely it is used is not available here.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q82874569&quot;>Wikidata Q82874569</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>foslevodopa and decarboxylase inhibitor</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N04BA07</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB16683&quot;>DB16683</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:192509&quot;>192509</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q82874569&quot;>Q82874569</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C9H12NO7P</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>277.169 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
